From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:52:02 +0000
Subject: Skip early navigation for custom tabs outside the regular profile

When another app opens a link in a custom tab, LaunchIntentDispatcher can
start loading the page early in a hidden tab that was prepared in advance.
That tab always belongs to the regular profile, so the early navigation
sends the regular profile's cookies and can store site data there. A
custom tab that opens in another profile does not use the hidden tab and
loads the page again.

Skip the early navigation in every case in which the custom tab does not
open in the regular profile: in always-incognito mode; when the tab opens
in incognito or in an ephemeral profile because of the option to open
external links in incognito or because the app asked for it and the
request is accepted, the only case skipped before; and with the
MayLaunchUrlUsesSeparateStoragePartition feature, with which this browser
opens custom tabs other than Auth Tabs in an ephemeral profile (it is off
by default). In those cases the page starts loading slightly later.

An incognito request from an app is now judged with the calling app's
package, which the custom tab also uses to accept it. An app that is
identified only by that package therefore no longer gets an early
navigation in the regular profile while its tab opens in incognito.

